== Scoring Criteria

Each criterion is scored by the level that best describes the project. Choose the Excellent, Adequate, or Incomplete descriptor, then record the points earned in the score sheet below.

#table(
  columns: (1.3fr, 0.7fr, 2fr, 2fr, 2fr),
  align: (left, center, left, left, left),
  [*Criterion*], [*Points*], [*Excellent*], [*Adequate*], [*Incomplete*],
  [Question and Hypothesis], [10],
  [Question is clear, testable, and focused. Hypothesis is specific and states an expected relationship between variables.],
  [Question is testable but broad. Hypothesis is present but vague or lacks a stated reason.],
  [Question is missing or not testable. No hypothesis is stated.],
  [Background Research], [10],
  [Cites several credible sources. Explains the science clearly and connects it to the hypothesis.],
  [Cites a few sources. Explains basic concepts but connections to the project are weak.],
  [Few or no sources. Little or no explanation of the underlying science.],
  [Experimental Design and Variables], [20],
  [Identifies independent, dependent, and controlled variables. Includes repeated trials and a control. Procedure is detailed enough to replicate.],
  [Identifies most variables. Procedure is mostly clear but missing some controls or details.],
  [Variables are unclear or unidentified. Procedure is incomplete or cannot be replicated.],
  [Data Collection and Record Keeping], [15],
  [Data is accurate, organized, and recorded consistently with correct units. Uses a log or table throughout.],
  [Data is mostly complete with minor errors or inconsistent units. Records are partially organized.],
  [Data is missing, disorganized, or unreliable. Units are absent or incorrect.],
  [Analysis and Conclusion], [20],
  [Graphs or charts are accurate and labeled. Results are interpreted correctly. Conclusion addresses the hypothesis, notes sources of error, and suggests improvements.],
  [Graphs are present with some labeling issues. Conclusion addresses the hypothesis but explanation of error or next steps is limited.],
  [Graphs are missing or incorrect. Conclusion does not match the data or ignores the hypothesis.],
  [Display Board and Written Report], [15],
  [Board is neat, logical, and easy to read. Report includes all required sections and is free of major errors.],
  [Board is readable with some disorganization. Report includes most required sections with several errors.],
  [Board is hard to follow or incomplete. Report is missing sections or contains many errors.],
  [Oral Presentation], [10],
  [Speaks clearly and confidently. Explains the project in logical order and answers questions accurately.],
  [Speaks adequately. Explains most of the project and answers some questions correctly.],
  [Speech is unclear or rushed. Struggles to explain the project or answer questions.],
  [Scientific Creativity and Effort], [10],
  [Project shows original thinking, independent work, and clear personal investment beyond the basic assignment.],
  [Project shows some original thinking and moderate effort beyond the basic assignment.],
  [Project largely follows a template or example with little original thinking or effort.],
)

